      "writtenOn": "2014-09-07T15:40:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nah, we should ensure that we release connection we\u0027ve acquired from parent pool. Otherwise this connection will just leak and pool capacity will shrink. It\u0027s like we had this logic with the parent class:\n\n    conn \u003d pool.acquire()\n    try:\n        \u003cdo_smth\u003e\n    finally:\n        pool.release(conn)\n\nAnd now we want to put smth before try: block. We need to be sure we either enter try: block and finally: block gets executed or we release connection ourselves on any error.\n\nAlthough there should be no exceptions here at all, I\u0027d prefer to avoid possible leakage.",
      "parentUuid": "fa98f980_3b992b20",
      "revId": "7a5367ccbd34a05bc8b63266e14952e926b9731b",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
